{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"0448c3e2c5a8b8119736a77c66700dc6f43998721f4d1729aaa207c81963bdef","slug":"book.grain-of-salt.2026-08-31-economics-minor","location":"/book/grain-of-salt/2026-08-31-economics-minor.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Why Every Undergraduate Should Consider a Minor (if not Major) in Economics","description":"A personal essay on why an economics minor (or major) pays off in earnings, versatility, and an AI-era toolkit.","short_title":"Economics minor","date":"2026-08-31","content_includes_title":false,"copyright":"2026","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"thumbnail":"/build/economics-minor-inco-e9e7b126420f91ab8ef7eb99d5e8b260.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"2026-08-31-economics-minor.md","url":"/build/2026-08-31-economics-41c687eea85adbb9523f7323d21f7217.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choosing a minor in college can shape not only a student’s academic journey but also their long-term career trajectory and personal growth. Economics, in particular, stands out as one of the most valuable minors an undergraduate can pursue. Here’s why:","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"htzONar9uL"}],"key":"fVst27gt4m"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Economics Graduates Are Among the Highest Earners","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"KndR5S1kaW"}],"identifier":"id-1-economics-graduates-are-among-the-highest-earners","label":"1. Economics Graduates Are Among the Highest Earners","html_id":"id-1-economics-graduates-are-among-the-highest-earners","implicit":true,"key":"XAzibPSh8I"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"According to data compiled by Waldron (2024), economics majors consistently rank at the top for lifetime earnings among all undergraduate fields. The study highlights that students who major or minor in economics maximize their lifetime net worth. This earning potential is not just a short-term trend; it persists across decades and sectors.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"q9elC0isX9"}],"key":"sGFpuFWmWb"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/economics-minor-inco-e9e7b126420f91ab8ef7eb99d5e8b260.png","alt":"Two scatter plots of 2024 ACS income by college major, with economics highlighted on mean income, skewness, and standard deviation.","key":"CCEGzW9qYG","urlSource":"../images/economics-minor-income-by-major.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Income by college major from the 2024 American Community Survey, with economics highlighted. Source: ","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"tPVJebkT9b"},{"type":"link","url":"https://economistwritingeveryday.com/2026/08/28/income-by-major-acs-2024","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Income by major, ACS 2024","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"XOI7dc4r69"}],"urlSource":"https://economistwritingeveryday.com/2026/08/28/income-by-major-acs-2024","key":"xFqA99s0vK"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"t4fZPQhqxA"}],"key":"tvXUZk2Cn2"}],"key":"LPi7c9Umbd"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"uAQm4aiNtA"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source: ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"x6oQ4nmgwb"},{"type":"link","url":"https://economistwritingeveryday.com/2026/08/28/income-by-major-acs-2024","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://​economistwritingeveryday​.com​/2026​/08​/28​/income​-by​-major​-acs​-2024","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"jG3UIZWyAq"}],"urlSource":"https://economistwritingeveryday.com/2026/08/28/income-by-major-acs-2024","key":"qiLZvsKlBi"}],"key":"XqgfzoeYQq"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Economics Degree Leads to Wealth Accumulation","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"DdJ3ayrUjK"}],"identifier":"id-2-economics-degree-leads-to-wealth-accumulation","label":"2. Economics Degree Leads to Wealth Accumulation","html_id":"id-2-economics-degree-leads-to-wealth-accumulation","implicit":true,"key":"i5fe9zQVai"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recent data reveals a striking trend in wealth creation: 23% of America’s top 100 billionaires share the same undergraduate major. Surprisingly, this degree is neither business nor a specialized MBA. Instead, it is economics, a field available at nearly every institution. While business programs often focus on the tactical “how-to” of corporate management, economics provides a superior foundation for wealth accumulation by fostering a systemic understanding of how markets and incentives operate at their core.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"KV0Bn245q0"}],"key":"SBTUH1LkT7"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Economics outperforms traditional business degrees because it prioritizes first principles over current corporate trends. By training students to think in terms of opportunity costs, marginal utility, and game theory, economics develops an analytical mindset that allows individuals to identify value where others see noise. This rigorous, quantitative approach to human behavior and resource allocation equips future leaders to navigate complex global systems with a level of critical foresight that purely vocational business training rarely replicates.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"OMPN3wN25F"}],"key":"ddZaYOs7H4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source: ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"Lb6Np3D2Xf"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/billconerly/2021/06/19/billionaires-undergraduate-majors-economics-topped-the-list/","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"forbes.com","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"s9i9YMw7rw"}],"urlSource":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/billconerly/2021/06/19/billionaires-undergraduate-majors-economics-topped-the-list/","key":"juk1X94Dvs"}],"key":"ga175WJEus"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Economists: The Ultimate Generalist-Specialists","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"kc28wwqLLj"}],"identifier":"id-3-economists-the-ultimate-generalist-specialists","label":"3. Economists: The Ultimate Generalist-Specialists","html_id":"id-3-economists-the-ultimate-generalist-specialists","implicit":true,"key":"WjXGTmDIEQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Economics is unique in that it produces both generalists and specialists. Economists are trained to think broadly about complex systems (generalist) and to analyze data or policies with precision (specialist). This duality makes them adaptable and highly valued in diverse roles from finance and consulting to public policy, tech, and healthcare. The skillset is so versatile that it’s often hard to define exactly what an economist does if you enjoy a challenge and crave versatility, economics is the field for you.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"NXfI38fIRX"}],"key":"JPSXKzK0SL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source:","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"CuyM3saEMA"}],"key":"lDVEykMSTd"},{"type":"text","value":" ","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"qEG1m4ROGN"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.aeaweb.org/resources/students/careers","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"American Economic Association: Careers in Economics","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"D43GLNAQiJ"}],"urlSource":"https://www.aeaweb.org/resources/students/careers","key":"rRGDfZsZJg"}],"key":"Z86WtSgjhH"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Beyond the Balance Sheet: Why Economics Matters Everywhere","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"jf10quqVfy"}],"identifier":"id-4-beyond-the-balance-sheet-why-economics-matters-everywhere","label":"4. Beyond the Balance Sheet: Why Economics Matters Everywhere","html_id":"id-4-beyond-the-balance-sheet-why-economics-matters-everywhere","implicit":true,"key":"XZiOYIPtAR"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A common misconception is that economics is strictly confined to the stock market, monetary policy, or high-level finance. In reality, the field is significantly broader, offering a framework to understand how people make choices under scarcity. It is often described as the “queen of the social sciences” because it utilizes logic and quantitative methods to study human behavior and complex systems. This analytical toolkit is applicable across nearly every conceivable domain, including health, education, law, and environmental science.","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"U4EaAUuIEC"}],"key":"nySmb8CoeZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The interdisciplinary success of economics is best illustrated by the diverse paths of its practitioners. For instance, ","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"oCODmdrRWM"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marcella Alsan","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"cYjmLgsE9X"}],"key":"dpjrnySKZ0"},{"type":"text","value":", a physician of infectious diseases, pursued an economics degree to better understand the systemic barriers affecting her patients’ health outcomes. In the private sector, ","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"Z1qrkpGQpG"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Randall Lewis","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"ruLSUv0oYN"}],"key":"mKRvsPUXUX"},{"type":"text","value":" has utilized economic theory at Google and Amazon to optimize market performance through large-scale data analysis. Additionally, researchers like ","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"ndLi0cm8Gx"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Britni Wilcher","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"yJ1Zl27adm"}],"key":"birnkrIPuU"},{"type":"text","value":" work to dispel myths about the field, highlighting how economic considerations guide professional decisions in academia and beyond.","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"clCXWwdMg0"}],"key":"h88ZDr283P"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"From agriculture and computer science to journalism and psychology, economics provides a lens to decode the incentives and tradeoffs that drive the world. By simplifying complex interactions into understandable concepts, an economics background empowers individuals to excel in any field they choose.","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"D19MsQJZAH"}],"key":"k6Jbv2YWUp"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Healthier, Happier, Smarter, and More Impactful","position":{"start":{"line":47,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"key":"WPRVwLWDXn"}],"identifier":"id-5-healthier-happier-smarter-and-more-impactful","label":"5. Healthier, Happier, Smarter, and More Impactful","html_id":"id-5-healthier-happier-smarter-and-more-impactful","implicit":true,"key":"G6qNXTpKin"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Healthier:","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"raHmPdqGQ8"}],"key":"X2CQhZ9k61"},{"type":"text","value":" Economic literacy is linked to better personal finance management, reduced stress from money issues, and access to better healthcare choices (Lusardi & Mitchell, 2014).","position":{"start":{"line":49,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"key":"JI0Wb0fMNK"}],"key":"p2o8nXjZgx"}],"key":"msHWJzWAgU"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Happier:","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"Y9pmbWfytR"}],"key":"CAxofiijQz"},{"type":"text","value":" Surveys show that economics graduates report higher levels of job satisfaction, autonomy, and career flexibility (National Survey of College Graduates, NSF).","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"p6oi728GWw"}],"key":"psiCxFufcZ"}],"key":"lcW2xJqt53"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Smarter:","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"rev55HE6Sa"}],"key":"rGKq9Q0V0b"},{"type":"text","value":" Economics fosters critical thinking, quantitative reasoning, and data literacy: skills at the heart of innovation and leadership (Goldin & Katz, 2008).","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"KuUM94XGsP"}],"key":"oehhAqVMtM"}],"key":"ajtEnScKww"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wealthier:","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"AnMZ1iqKRM"}],"key":"JElqQzeYV0"},{"type":"text","value":" As noted, no other major has a stronger correlation with long-term wealth accumulation.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"UVaSaWArlY"}],"key":"b2LLQDeHur"}],"key":"BS9H2AF5Fi"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"More Impactful:","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"EofIfAC55q"}],"key":"TxnuY3XNUF"},{"type":"text","value":" Economists shape policies that affect millions, drive business strategies, and tackle global challenges like climate change, inequality, and healthcare reform.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"TCNfwZiv2C"}],"key":"bJXO53zFDV"}],"key":"gVHxvtHlTJ"}],"key":"Sfa8tHlrIv"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/economics-minor-earn-431f080faf8b53c35a0880519757ab89.jpg","alt":"Horizontal bar chart of the highest- and lowest-paid college majors by synthetic work-life earnings, with economics at the top.","key":"SfQdEbH5CU","urlSource":"../images/economics-minor-earnings-gap.jpg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":