ntext and assess strategic trade-offs is more critical than ever. Economics equips students with a “toolkit for reality,” allowing them to navigate shifting markets with agility. According to the Future of Jobs Report (World Economic Forum, 2024), analytical thinking and systems analysis, the core pillars of economic training, remain the most sought-after skills by global employers. By learning to model complex human incentives, economics minors gain a competitive edge that technology cannot easily replicate, ensuring long-term professional resilience.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"onJKQMRztg"}],"key":"TEsxjnVq9j"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A minor in economics isn’t just a credential: it’s an investment in a more prosperous, flexible, and impactful future. Whether your primary interest is in business, policy, STEM, or the arts, the analytical toolkit and career outcomes of economics will set you apart.","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"qBXdYVgat4"}],"key":"NgwyAm9bHm"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"References","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"NgNkVrQvtn"}],"identifier":"references","label":"References","html_id":"references","implicit":true,"key":"j5Oz0oEmz3"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Waldron, J. (2024). The College Earnings Gap Isn’t One. Retrieved from ","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"LW76mj9